section: compiler
synopsis:
  ``-fno-cpr-anal`` now switches off CPR analysis itself, rather than just
  stopping worker/wrapper from using its results.
issues: #28187
mrs: !17063
description: {
  Previously CPR analysis ran whenever worker/wrapper was enabled, regardless
  of ``-fcpr-anal``. Now each of the demand analyser, CPR analyser and
  worker/wrapper passes is controlled by its own flag:

  - Demand analysis runs if ``-fstrictness`` is on.
  - CPR analysis runs if both ``-fcpr-anal`` and ``-fworker-wrapper`` are on.
  - Worker/wrapper runs if ``-fworker-wrapper`` is on and at least one of
    the two analyses has run.

  One consequence is that a module compiled with ``-fno-cpr-anal`` has no
  CPR information in its interface file, so CPR analysis in importing
  modules sees less. Also, ``-fno-strictness -fworker-wrapper`` now runs CPR
  analysis and worker/wrapper, where previously it ran neither.
}
